    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239-a2">

                <pb facs="0697" n="483" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg483"/>

                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1871-09-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 6, 1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 31st ultimo, acquainting me that the President of the United
                    States has appointed the Hon. Charles Francis Adams, of Massachusetts, as the
                    arbitrator to be named by him under Article I of the treaty of Washington of May
                    8, on the tribunal of arbitration to meet at Geneva in December next.</p>
                <pb facs="0698" n="484" xml:id="pg484"/>
                <p>I beg to take this opportunity of informing you that the Right Honorable Sir
                    Alexander Cockburn, baronet, the Lord Chief Justice of Queen’s Bench, has been
                    appointed by Her Majesty the Queen in a similar capacity.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GRANVILLE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Benjamin Moran</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
